            <ArticleTitle>Surgical strategy for subepicardial aneurysm: two case reports.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>291-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Subepicardial aneurysm is a rare complication of acute myocardial infarction (AMI) and is associated with the risk of spontaneous rupture. We present two patients with subepicardial aneurysms detected after 1 day and 6 weeks after AMI. Both lesions were successfully treated by patch repair.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
